            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LinZ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was making this 40+ years ago for my kids as a veggie dip. Now I use horseradish mustard, and I omit the vinegar and add dill relish and a little of the liquid. I used to love Thousand Island Dressing for salads, burgers and veggie dipping, but this is WAY better with the dill relish instead of the sweet relish in the dressing. Also great on hot dogs, sandwiches and tuna salad, and in place of tarter and cocktail sauce. 4 stars for the basic and 5 stars with the dill relish.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-18T23:39:21.404Z"
          },
